{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQ8P9e1vL5ooP9wDYDnj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**BROS gross profit in 2026 comes out at about $467 million** under your assumptions.\n\n**FY2024 starting point** (10-K for FY2024):\n- Revenue: $1,281.0M\n- Cost of sales: $940.9M\n- Gross profit: $340.1M, which is a gross margin of **26.55%**\n\n**Assumptions applied:**\n- Revenue grows 30% a year for two years: $1,281.0M × 1.30² (1.69) = **$2,164.9M** in 2026\n- Gross margin falls by 500bps: 26.55% − 5.00% = **21.55%**\n\n**2026 gross profit:** $2,164.9M × 21.55% ≈ **$466.6M, or about $467M**\n\nNotes:\n- Dutch Bros does not report a gross profit line. I calculated it as revenue minus the \"cost of sales\" figure it reports. That cost line includes most shop-level operating costs, which is why the margin is lower than you might expect.\n- As instructed, I used only filings dated on or before 16 May 2025. Newer data in EDGAR, including the FY2025 10-K filed 2026-02-13, was left out.\n\n**Sources**\n- Dutch Bros Inc. Form 10-K for FY2024, filed 2025-02-13, accession 0001866581-25-000048 (XBRL: RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax, CostOfGoodsAndServicesSold)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3221,"cache_read_input_tokens":9595,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3221},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b65b5a55-f043-4cf5-9904-47713bdbc915","uuid":"32911c78-f7a0-48fb-a210-01726a1f43fc","timestamp":"2026-10-26T03:20:30.962Z","request_id":"req_011CgQ8P9NQEz7NWVoweubrr"}
